R"VG(
# census_obituary.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the census return (a household of the history: `@cast household`, its head `$x` with
# the spouse and the child the history gives them, the house as the ruins show it), the railway's timetable (once the railway runs:
# `railway`), the obituary (a death the chronicle told: `@cast notable`; its epithet, its trade, its cause). The voice on a wax cylinder
# is voice.vg's.

@root obit.deed.* obit.by.*

# ---- the census return -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
genre.census (words=34..120)
  {@cast household}{census.head}\n{census.head2}\n{census.row.x}\n{census.row.sp}\n{census.row.ch}\n{census.end}
  {@cast household}{census.head}\n{census.head2}\n{census.row.x}\n{census.row.sp}\n{census.row.ch}\n{census.row.more}\n{census.end} {census.end2}

census.head (formula)
  The count of the people, year {#year:digits}. The return of one house at {$x.home}.
  Census of {$x.home}, the {#year:ord} year of {city}: a household.
  The {#year:ord} year of {city}: the count of the people of {$x.home}, sheet {n}.

census.head2 (formula)
  Name, place in the house, age, trade.
  Name; place in the house; age; trade or calling.

census.row.x
  {$x:name}, head of the house, {#$x.age}, {$x.trade}.
census.row.sp
  (has:$x.spouse) {$x.spouse:name}, {census.spword}, {#$x.spouse.age}, {$x.spouse.trade}.
  (!has:$x.spouse) No wife or husband living.
census.spword
  ($x.spouse.gender=she) wife
  ($x.spouse.gender=he) husband
census.row.ch
  (has:$x.child) {$x.child:name}, {census.chword}, {#$x.child.age}, {census.chtrade}.
census.chword
  ($x.child.gender=she) daughter
  ($x.child.gender=he) son
census.chtrade
  ($x.child.age<5) at home
  ($x.child.age>=5 $x.child.age<12) at school
  ($x.child.age>=12) {$x.child.trade}
census.row.more
  A lodger, name not given, [nineteen|twenty-two|thirty|forty-one], a hand at the {craft} works.
  A servant girl, fourteen, from the hills.
  An apprentice, {census.appr}, sleeps in the shop.
  The head's mother, very old, takes in sewing.
  Two lodgers, brothers, carters, rarely in.
census.appr
  fifteen
  sixteen
  thirteen, if the parents are to be believed

census.end
  Also living in the house: {n} lodgers, names not given.
  The house has {n} rooms and {census.water}.
  The house is {house.one}, under {roofs}.
  The enumerator notes that the head of the house would not give the ages of the lodgers.
  The family keep {n} {herd} in the yard and a {beast} in the kitchen.
  (stage>=1) The enumerator notes that the street is half empty.
  Signed by the head of the house, with a mark.
  The household speaks the tongue of the {people} at home, and the city's at work.
  The enumerator was given {drink} and asked to come back next year.
census.end2
  Religion: {census.faith}.
  Rent: {n} {coin} the quarter, paid.
  The enumerator notes {census.note}.
census.water
  water from {watersrc}
  no water but what is carried
  (age>=industrial) a tap in the yard, which works
  a share of the pump with three other houses
census.faith
  (faith=ancestors) the old ones of the family
  (faith=land) the spirits of the land, and the chapel at {festival}
  (faith=sky) the sky, as the old people keep it
  (faith=manygods) {god} and the others
  (faith=onegod) {god}
  (faith=philosophy) none, by conviction
  (faith=machine) as the law requires
  none given
census.note
  a dog that would not let him in
  that the children were counted twice, having moved during the count
  that the head is the oldest {$x.trade} in the street
  a smell of {fuel} and {food}

# ---- the railway's timetable ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
genre.timetable (words=29..125)
  {tt.head}\n{tt.row}\n{tt.row}\n{tt.row}\n{tt.note}
  {tt.head}\n{tt.row}\n{tt.row}\n{tt.row}\n{tt.row}\n{tt.note} {tt.note2}

tt.head (formula)
  The {city} railway. Trains from {$home}, {season.now}, year {#year:digits}.
  Timetable of the line through {$home}, in force from the first of {season.now}.
  Departures from {$home}, {season.now} service, the {#year:ord} year of {city}.

tt.row
  (once) To {tt.dest}: {tt.when}{tt.more}.
  (once) To {tt.dest}: {tt.when}{tt.more}.
  (once) To {tt.dest}: {tt.when}{tt.more}.
  (once homerank!=capital) To {city}: {tt.when}{tt.more}.
  (once) The goods train, with {tt.goods}: {tt.goods.when}.
  (once) The mail: {tt.mail}, not for passengers.
  (once) Market specials: {tt.market}.
tt.dest (people=6)
  the coast
  the hill towns
  the junction
  the mines
  the border
  the river towns
  the south
  the north
  the {crop} country
  the market towns
  the foot of {mountain}
  the quarries
  the lakes
  the old capital
tt.when
  first light and at noon
  once a day, at the second bell
  twice a day, stopping everywhere
  every hour until dark
  {time.of}, and on rest days not at all
  at the {nth} bell and again at lamp-lighting
  three times a day in {season.now}, once in {season.next}
tt.more
  ; the journey takes a day and a night
  ; change at the junction for the hill line
  ; through carriages on market days
  , the evening train on rest days only
  ; {herd} in the rear van only
  , returning the next morning
  ; the fare is {n} {coin}, third class
tt.goods
  {crop} and {vessel}
  {herd} and {fuel}
  the {craft} works' loads
  {fruit} in season
tt.goods.when
  when it comes
  at night, and noisily
  on the {nth} day of the week
  daily but for the rest day
tt.mail
  at night
  at the {nth} bell
  {time.of}
tt.market
  on the eve of every market, with room for {herd}
  in {festival} week, three a day each way
  for the {crop} harvest, as required

tt.note
  Passengers are asked not to ride on the roofs, nor to carry {herd} in the carriages.
  Fares are to be paid at the window and not to the guard, in {coin} and not in {crop}.
  The company is not responsible for the weather, nor for {weather.now} in {season.now}.
  (stage>=1) Some trains on this list no longer run. Ask at the window.
  Passengers with {herd} will travel with them, in the van.
  The company regrets the changes, which are the council's fault.
  Children under {n} travel free, on a lap; {tt.beasts} by arrangement.
  On {festival} the trains run all night, and so do the passengers.
tt.note2
  Lost property is kept at {$home} station for one month, then given to {holyplace}.
  Smoking is permitted in the end carriages only, and {drink} nowhere.
  The station clock is right; the passengers are early or late.
  Refreshments at the station: {food} and {drink}, at station prices.

# ---- the obituary ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
genre.obituary (words=23..100)
  {@cast notable}{obit.head}\n{obit.life}\n{@deed obit.deed}\n{@death obit.by}\n{obit.end}
  {@cast notable}{obit.head}\n{obit.life} {obit.more}\n{@deed obit.deed}\n{@death obit.by}\n{obit.end}

obit.head (formula)
  ($x.role=ruler) {$x:full}, {#$x.born:digits} to {#$x.died:digits}.
  ($x.role!=ruler) {$x:name}, {$x.trade}, of {$x.home}.
  Deaths: {$x:name}.
  ($x.role=ruler has:$x.epithet) {$x:name} {$x.epithet}.
  In memoriam: {$x:name} of {$x.home}.

obit.life
  Born in the {#$x.born:ord} year of {city}, {$x:name} lived {#$x.age|year}, most of them at {$x.home}.
  {$x:name} was {#$x.age} and had lived at {$x.home} all {$x:poss} life.
  ($x.role=ruler has:$x.reigned) {$x:name} held the rule {#$x.reigned|year}.
  ($x.role=general) {$x:name} led the army in the wars, and came home from most of them.
  ($x.role=maker|$x.role=inventor) {$x:name} was known to everyone at {$x.home} for {$x:poss} work.
  ($x.role=prophet) {$x:name} preached for many years, and many listened.
  (has:$x.trait) {$x:name} was {obit.trait.how} {$x.trait}, and at {$x.home} nobody needed to be told so.
  (has:$x.home.ptrade) {$x:name} lived at {$x.home}, which lives by {$x.home.ptrade}, and was part of it for {#$x.age|year}.
obit.trait.how
  thought
  known to be
  by every account
obit.more
  (has:$x.children) {$x:name} raised {#$x.children|child}.
  {$x:name} was seen every morning at {town.open}, and will be missed there.
  (has:$x.family) {$x:name} was of the {$x.family} family, long at {$x.home}.
  {$x:name} kept {herd} to the end, against the doctor's advice.

obit.deed.built
  {$x:name} was the maker of {$d.work} at {$d.place}.
  {$d.work} at {$d.place} was {$x:poss} work, and stands.
obit.deed.battle
  {$x:name} fought at {$d.place}.
  {$x:name} was at {$d.place} in the war, and did not talk about it.
obit.deed.invention
  It was {$x:name} who made {$d.invention}.
obit.deed.deed
  {$x:name} is remembered for {obit.deedword}.
obit.deed.founding
  {$x:name} saw the founding of {$d.place}.
obit.deed.trade
  {$x:name} was a {$x.trade} and a good one.
  {$x:name} worked as a {$x.trade} until the last year.
  {$x:name} was a {$x.trade} for {#$x.age:about|year}, and taught the trade to half the street.

obit.deedword
  ($d.deed=song) a song that everyone knows
  ($d.deed=book|$d.deed=chronicle) a book that everyone read
  ($d.deed=theory) a new account of the world
  ($d.deed=taught) the years of teaching
  ($d.deed!=song $d.deed!=book $d.deed!=chronicle $d.deed!=theory $d.deed!=taught) what was done at {$d.place}

obit.by.sickness
  {$x:name} died of {$c.sickness}, at {$x.home}.
  {$c.sickness} took {$x:name} in {season.now}.
obit.by.battle
  {$x:name} fell at {$c.place}.
obit.by.famine
  {$x:name} died in the hungry year.
obit.by.flood
  {$x:name} was drowned in the flood at {$c.place}.
obit.by.quake
  {$x:name} died when the ground shook at {$c.place}.
obit.by.old
  {$x:name} died quietly, at home, after a short illness.
  {$x:name} died in {$x:poss} sleep, at a great age.
obit.by.illness
  {$x:name} died after a long illness, bravely borne.
obit.by.young
  {$x:name} died young, and the town has not got over it.
obit.by.childbirth
  {$x:name} died in childbirth; the child lives.
obit.by.accident
  {$x:name} died in an accident at the works.
obit.by.sea
  {$x:name} was lost at sea.
obit.by.cold
  {$x:name} died in the great cold.
obit.by.fire
  {$x:name} died in a fire.
obit.by.any
  {$x:name} died at {$x.home}.

obit.end
  The burying is at {deadplace} tomorrow; all are welcome.
  (has:$x.spouse) {$x.spouse:name} and the family ask that no flowers be sent.
  The family thank all who sent word.
  (has:$x.child) {$x:name} leaves {$x.child:name} and others.
  The shops of {$x.home} will close for the funeral, as they have not for anyone in years.
  Friends will wear {colour.mourn} for {n} days, as was asked.
tt.beasts
  dogs
  birds in cages
  small beasts
)VG"
